Upstream implementation base
----------------------------
Portions of the RouterOS binary framing/streaming design are adapted from:

SourceRegistry/mikrotik-client
https://github.com/SourceRegistry/mikrotik-client
Baseline commit: 4b2869c97f287bfef3f9fa03803bbe1b1b96a92b
License: Apache-2.0

The adapted portions have been substantially refactored and hardened for this
project, including stricter `!empty`/`!done` lifecycle handling, independent
`/cancel` tag tracking, bounded stream buffers, protocol resource limits,
conservative ambiguous-write semantics, and Node.js 24.19 networking behavior.

Comparative implementation reference
------------------------------------
@fibercom/routeros-api 2.0.0 is used as a functional/reference benchmark for
fragmented decoding, tagged concurrency, streaming, TLS, legacy compatibility,
and public API design. No Fibercom source code is incorporated by this notice.
License of that reference package: MIT.

Protocol/runtime authority
--------------------------
When implementations disagree, MikroTik's official RouterOS API documentation
is authoritative for protocol behavior, and the official Node.js documentation
is authoritative for runtime/socket semantics. Real RouterOS/CHR conformance
tests are required before stable releases.
